y is SEBC/OEC)\n- EWS Certificate (if admitted category is EWS)\n- Caste/Community Certificate (if admitted category is SC/ST/Jews)\n- Migration Certificate (for boards other than HSC/VHSC)\n- Pass Certificate of the qualifying examination (if issued)\n- Any other certificate of eligibility, if allotment is under any other quotas like CC, PT, XS, SD, DK, RP, JW, SGETC.\n- No Objection Certificate (NOC) from their present institution.\n- Plus 2 Mark Sheet\n- Data Sheet issued by CEE\n- SSLC/10th Certificate\n- Certificate to prove date of birth in original (SSLC/Birth Certificate/Valid Indian Passport)\n- Proof of Nativity in original (SSLC/Birth Certificate/Valid Indian Passport or any valid document as per KEAM Prospectus 2025)\n- Non-Creamy layer Certificate (if admitted category is SEBC/OEC)\n- EWS Certificate (if admitted category is EWS)\n- Caste/Community Certificate (if admitted category is SC/ST/Jews)\n- Transfer Certificate (Students without TC will not be permitted to join) (For Fresh Admissions)\n- Conduct Certificate (For Fresh Admissions)\n- Physical Fitness Certificate in the relevant format given in the prospectus 2026.\n- Pass Certificate of the qualifying examination (if issued)\n- Any other certificate of eligibility, if allotment is under any other quotas like CC, PT, XS, SD, DK, RP, JW, SGETC."
